# E.A.S.E.M Usage Guide

## Enhanced Administration and System Environment Manager

---

## Master Control Commands

### Main Interface

```bash
cd easem/master

# Show help
./easem-master.sh help

# Initialize system
./easem-master.sh init

# Check status
./easem-master.sh status

# Launch interactive menu
./easem-master.sh menu
```

---

## Dashboard & Monitoring

### View All Clients

```bash
# List all configured clients with status
./easem-dashboard.sh list
```

Output shows:
- Client name
- Username
- Host/IP address
- SSH port
- Online/Offline status (color-coded)

### Live Monitoring Dashboard

```bash
# Start live dashboard (auto-refresh every 3 seconds)
./easem-dashboard.sh live
```

Shows real-time:
- CPU usage percentage
- Memory (total, used, free, percentage)
- Disk usage
- System load (1, 5, 15 min averages)
- Uptime
- Process count
- Network interface stats

Press `Ctrl+C` to exit.

### Single Client View

```bash
# View specific client metrics once
./easem-dashboard.sh show laptop2

# View all clients once (no auto-refresh)
./easem-dashboard.sh all
```

---

## Remote Command Execution

### Execute Single Command

```bash
# Using master control
./easem-master.sh exec laptop2 "df -h"

# Using commands script directly
./easem-commands.sh john 192.168.1.105 "uptime" 22
```

### Common Commands

```bash
# Check disk space
./easem-master.sh exec laptop2 "df -h"

# View running processes
./easem-master.sh exec laptop2 "ps aux | head -10"

# Check system uptime
./easem-master.sh exec laptop2 "uptime"

# List installed packages
./easem-master.sh exec laptop2 "apt list --installed | grep python"

# Check network connections
./easem-master.sh exec laptop2 "ss -tuln"

# View memory usage
./easem-master.sh exec laptop2 "free -h"
```

### Command Validation

For security, commands are validated before execution:
- Dangerous commands (rm -rf, mkfs, dd, fork bombs) are blocked
- Commands are logged for audit trail
- Whitelist system can be customized in `shared/easem-security.sh`

---

## Package Installation

### Install Package on Client

```bash
# Install single package
./easem-master.sh install laptop2 htop

# Install multiple packages
./easem-master.sh exec laptop2 "sudo apt install -y vim git curl"
```

The system will:
1. Check if apt is available
2. Update package list
3. Install the requested package
4. Show installation output

---

## Chat Feature

### List Available Chats

```bash
# Show all clients and unread message count
./easem-chat.sh list
```

### Start Chat Session

```bash
# Start chatting with a client
./easem-chat.sh start laptop2

# Or using master control
./easem-master.sh chat laptop2 start
```

Chat Interface:
- Messages auto-refresh every 1 second
- Master messages shown in green
- Client messages shown in blue
- Type message and press Enter to send

### Chat Commands

During chat session:
- `:exit` - Exit chat session
- `:clear` - Clear screen (keeps history)
- Any text - Send message

### View Chat History

```bash
# View last 50 messages
./easem-chat.sh history laptop2

# View last 100 messages
./easem-chat.sh history laptop2 100
```

---

## Client-Side Usage

On client machines, the agent provides local commands:

### Agent Status

```bash
cd ~/easem/agent

# Show agent status
./easem-agent.sh status
```

### View Local Metrics

```bash
# Display system metrics
./easem-agent.sh metrics

# Get JSON format
./easem-collector.sh --json
```

### Start Chat Client

```bash
# Start chat interface
./easem-chat-client.sh start

# View chat history
./easem-chat-client.sh history
```

This allows clients to:
- Initiate conversations with master
- Respond to messages
- View message history

