## Common Workflows

### Daily Monitoring

```bash
# Quick check of all systems
./easem-dashboard.sh list

# Monitor specific client
./easem-dashboard.sh show laptop2

# Start live monitoring
./easem-dashboard.sh live
```

### System Maintenance

```bash
# Update all clients
for client in laptop2 laptop3; do
    ./easem-master.sh exec $client "sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y"
done

# Check disk space on all
./easem-dashboard.sh all | grep -i "disk"

# Restart service on client
./easem-master.sh exec laptop2 "sudo systemctl restart nginx"
```

### Communication

```bash
# List clients with unread messages
./easem-chat.sh list

# Start chat with client
./easem-chat.sh start laptop2

# Review conversation history
./easem-chat.sh history laptop2
```

### Adding New Client

```bash
# 1. Setup SSH keys
./easem-deploy.sh --setup-ssh username host

# 2. Deploy agent
./easem-deploy.sh clientname username host 22

# 3. Verify connection
./easem-dashboard.sh show clientname

# 4. Test command execution
./easem-master.sh exec clientname "whoami"
```

---

## Tips & Best Practices

1. **SSH Keys:** Always use SSH key authentication for security and automation
2. **Client Names:** Use descriptive, unique names for easy identification
3. **Regular Monitoring:** Run live dashboard during demonstrations
4. **Chat Logs:** Chat history is persistent across sessions
5. **Command Safety:** Test commands on one client before running on multiple
6. **Network:** Ensure all machines are on the same network for WSL2 demos
7. **Backups:** Keep backup of `config/clients.list` and chat logs

---

## Troubleshooting

### Dashboard Shows Offline

```bash
# Test SSH connection
ssh username@host "echo OK"

# Check SSH service on client
ssh username@host "sudo service ssh status"

# Verify client in clients.list
cat config/clients.list | grep clientname
```

### Command Execution Fails

```bash
# Check command validation
# Ensure command is not in blocked list (see shared/easem-security.sh)

# Test command locally on client first
ssh username@host "your-command"

# Check logs for errors
./easem-master.sh logs master
```

### Chat Not Syncing

```bash
# Check chat directory exists on both sides
ls -la ../chat-data/
ssh username@host "ls -la ~/easem/chat-data/"

# Manually sync test
scp ../chat-data/chat_*.log username@host:~/easem/chat-data/

# Check network connectivity
ping host
```

